contentText:
Japanese artist Nigo and BTS&#8217; j-hope have teamed up with Nike to debut a new exclusive style of the classic Air Force 1 World Tour sneaker. According to a release announcing the team-up , Nigo has worked with j-hope to remix a classic and &#8220;deliver on his signature hobicore aesthetic.&#8221;

&#8220;What began as mutual admiration evolved into a creative partnership rooted in rarified taste, artistry and design — brought to life through a vibrant expression of the 2001 Air Force 1, which Nigo and Nike designers reprised for his multi-season Air Force 1 journey,&#8221; reads the statement.

&#8220;I really like the harmony of the enamel material color that Nigo expressed. And the special shoelace details that I haven’t seen often bring out the charm of the sneakers even more. It’s so good,&#8221; said j-hope about the unique design of the shoe, which features a glossy Burnt Sunrise and Metallic gold leather upper, Chlorine Blue accents and, on the insole, a collection of motifs featuring &#8220;signature squirrel graphics that embody j-hope&#8217;s energetic spirit.&#8221;

The heel of the shoe and its tongue tag also feature co-branding with Nigo and j-hope&#8217;s names on them and, instead of standard cotton laces, the sneakers have braided, multicolor ropes that pick up on the overall color scheme.

&#8220;I think j-hope is one of the few people who can become a true ambassador for culture and help carry it forward to the next generation,” said Nigo in the announcement of the shoe that comes in a custom shoebox featuring a mix of the sneaker&#8217;s colorway and the men&#8217;s names in bold print above the Nike swoosh.

The Nike x Nigo x j-hope Air Force 1 will launch exclusively on Oct. 17 here , followed by a global launch on Oct. 22 on Nike&#8217;s SNKRS app and at select retail outlets.
